# Smart answer

A smart answer asks questions and uses the responses to route someone to a relevant outcome. [Official publishing guidance](https://design-guide.publishing.service.gov.uk/frontend-templates/smart-answer/).

**Reference pattern.** The examples document a local adaptation; they do not add a publishing backend or a new Home Assistant capability.

## Reuse the question contract

Use [question pages](../../patterns/question-pages.html#compose-the-task-without-replacing-its-owner) for input, back navigation and retained answers. This template adds a bounded route to explanatory outcomes. Its reference examples do not configure native triggers, conditions or actions, and must not be described as an implemented automation or diagnostic editor.

## When to use it

A bounded troubleshooting decision aid can help users find the right existing guidance. Ask one meaningful question at a time, include “I do not know” where appropriate and keep a route back to change an answer. Distinguish a suggested next check from a diagnosis.

## Structure and behaviour

Define every branch, outcome and prerequisite before building the interaction. Retain previous responses while moving backwards. Do not hide contradictory evidence or make a confident recommendation from an unavailable reading. Prefer a simple checklist when a decision tree adds no value.

## Home Assistant boundary

The theme provides no diagnostic engine and does not infer appliance faults. Example choices navigate to explanatory text, not service calls. Safety-related decisions and device capability claims require verified domain guidance; they are not generated from a visual pattern.

